 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Self-heating and rating",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Power in the resistor raises it above ambient by an amount fixed by the combined thermal resistance of part and board. Rated dissipation holds as long as the film stays at or below 155 °C. P70 is the rating at an ambient of 70 °C and falls linearly to zero at 155 °C; the higher rating at a terminal temperature of 105 °C also falls linearly to zero at 155 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Lifetime and drift",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Within the permissible limits the parts have no defined end of life. Resistance rises with operating time, and an application's functional life ends when that rise exceeds its limit. At P70 the change is at most 2.0 % after 1000 h and 4.0 % after 8000 h."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pulse load",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Single-pulse limits apply when the average power is near zero, fewer than 1000 pulses are applied and the pulse voltage stays within Ûmax. Continuous-pulse limits apply when the average power stays within the derated power for the ambient and the pulse voltage within Ûmax. Both limits are set so the resistance change matches that of 8000 h of operation."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "A cermet film with a glass layer over it is laid on both faces of an alumina (Al2O3) ceramic substrate that carries inner contacts on each face; the 0402 has its film on one face only, except the jumper. The value is set by laser trimming of the film, then the element gets a protective coat. Terminations are matte tin plated over nickel. Every resistor is tested before it goes into the tape."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Assembly",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "The parts suit automatic SMD placement and wave, reflow or vapour phase soldering to IEC 61760-1. The coating withstands common electronics cleaning solvents such as alcohols, esters and water-based solutions. Conformal coatings and potting need their own qualification for long-term stability. The pure tin finish works with both lead-free and tin-lead solder. Solderability is specified for 2 years from production or requalification; storage of up to 20 years is permitted. The plating has been tested for resistance to tin whiskers."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Qualification and materials",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Qualified to AEC-Q200 and tested where applicable to EN 140401-802, which calls up EN 60115-1, EN 60115-8 and the IEC 60068 environmental tests. The tests also cover most of the requirements of EIA/IS-703 and JIS-C-5201-1. Climatic category LCT / UCT / 56 (56 days of steady damp heat). Free of the substances banned by IEC 62474, GADSL and the REACH SVHC list, and compliant with ELV 2000/53/EC with Annex II, RoHS 2011/65/EU with 2015/863/EU and WEEE 2012/19/EU. A version with SnPb terminations exists under document 20115."
  }
 ],
